; Under infer_tolerance_from_cost, a cost adds the units' tolerance times
; its smallest number to its currency's tolerance, which rounds the units
; interpolated in that currency. beancount's grammar gives total braces a
; per-unit part of zero, so {{574.99 USD}} adds nothing and the gains round
; to the 0.01 USD the cash implies; a per-unit cost adds its share, so they
; keep their digits.
option "infer_tolerance_from_cost" "TRUE"
2020-01-01 open Assets:Invest
2020-01-01 open Assets:Cash
2020-01-01 open Income:Gains

2020-01-02 * "total braces: the per-unit part is zero, so the cost adds nothing"
  Assets:Invest  18.572 VWELX {{574.99 USD}}
  Assets:Cash   -575.00 USD
  Income:Gains

2020-01-03 * "per-unit cost: the cost adds its share"
  Assets:Invest  18.572 VWELX {30.96 USD}
  Assets:Cash   -575.00 USD
  Income:Gains

2020-01-04 * "compound cost: the smaller number counts"
  Assets:Invest  18.572 VWELX {0.01 # 574.80 USD}
  Assets:Cash   -575.00 USD
  Income:Gains
